# Error Handling

## Not-found pattern

```java
public Platform requireById(String id) {
  return findById(id)
      .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND));
}
```

## HTTP-mapped errors

- Use `ResponseStatusException` with appropriate `HttpStatus`
- Custom exception classes only when reused across multiple domains

## Existence checks

For any "must exist" lookup, use `.orElseThrow(...)` directly — do not manually check `isPresent` / `isEmpty`:

```java
// GOOD
Platform p = repo.findById(id)
    .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND));

// BAD
Optional<Platform> opt = repo.findById(id);
if (opt.isEmpty()) {
  throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
}
Platform p = opt.get();
```

## Never swallow exceptions

```java
// ❌ BAD
try { doWork(); } catch (Exception e) {}

// ✅ GOOD
try {
  doWork();
} catch (Exception e) {
  log.error("Failed to do work for id={}", id, e);
  throw e;
}
```

## Null-safe returns

- Return `Collections.emptyList()` instead of null for empty collections
- Use `Optional<T>` for single-entity lookups that may not exist
